STEP 2 -- designed: read the sFlow CLI surface before sending any command      PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: tools/qmark.py types `PREFIX ?`, reads the help, then clears the line with Ctrl-U.
  It never sends a carriage return, so nothing is executed.

    sflow ?                                  -> agent | collector | enable
    sflow agent ?                            -> ip | ipv6
    sflow agent ip ?                         -> A.B.C.D
    sflow collector ?                        -> id   (the index of the collector)
    sflow collector id ?                     -> <1-5>
    sflow collector id 1 ?                   -> ip | ipv6
    sflow collector id 1 ip ?                -> A.B.C.D
    sflow collector id 1 ip 10.38.22.33 ?    -> max-datagram-size | port | vrf | <cr>
    sflow collector id 1 ip 10.38.22.33 port ? -> <1-65535>  (default: 6343)
    sflow enable ?                           -> <cr>
    interface: sflow ?                       -> max-header-size | polling-interval | sampling-rate
    interface: sflow sampling-rate ?         -> <50-2147483647>   the mean rate N, 1 in N packets
    interface: sflow polling-interval ?      -> <1-16777215>  seconds
    interface: sflow max-header-size ?       -> <14-200>  (default: 128)

  Three facts a later tester should not have to rediscover.
  - The collector is addressed by INDEX, not by address: `sflow collector id <1-5> ip
    <A.B.C.D>`.  The form `sflow collector ip <addr>` is `% Unrecognized command`.
  - The lowest sampling rate the CLI accepts is 50, which is 1 in 50.  A bench cannot ask for
    1 in 1.
  - The `no` forms are NOT symmetric with the positive forms.  This was found the hard way,
    by a rejection:

awplus(config)# no sflow collector id 1 ip 10.38.22.33
                                       ^
    % Invalid input detected at '^' marker.

    and then read properly with qmark:

    no sflow collector id 1 ?   -> <cr>          the INDEX ONLY, with no address
    no sflow agent ip ?         -> <cr>          with no address either

    That rejection put one line in the device log, quoted in the HEALTH block above.  It is
    the tester's own command, not a product fault.
  => STEP 2 PASS: every CLI token this case later sent was read off the device first, with
     no command executed.  Three CLI shapes were recorded for the next run.

