        2000-frame burst, 120 s capture                                  0 samples
    2   a FRESH cycle: `sflow enable` with rate 500 -> burst             enabled leg correct;
        (2 samples, both CK44309ON2) -> `no sflow enable` -> burst,      0 datagrams after
        100 s capture                                                    the disable
    3   the same again, with `sflow polling-interval 20` restored, so    enabled leg correct
        the configuration at the moment of disable matched the           (3 flow + 4 counters,
        original exactly                                                 all CK44309ON3);
                                                                         0 datagrams after
                                                                         the disable
    4   the whole original sequence mirrored, including the mid-flight   burst B gave 4 samples,
        rate change 50 -> 500 while enabled, and the same 28 s gap       all CK44309B, at
        before the post-disable burst                                    1-in-500;
                                                                         0 datagrams after
                                                                         the disable

  The STEP 6 behaviour was seen once and did not reproduce in three enable-then-disable cycles,
  including one that mirrored the original sequence step for step.  It is reported as a
  measured fact with its full evidence, and as intermittent.

  DEFECT 2 of 2 -- one enable gave zero flow samples at a rate that had given 40.
  In cycle 4's first burst, `sflow sampling-rate 50` was set while disabled, then `sflow
  enable` was sent, then the same 2000-frame burst.  The capture held 3 counters samples and
  ZERO flow samples.  STEP 4 produced exactly 40 at the same rate with the same burst.  The
  agent was transmitting, which the counters samples prove.  The port's rate read 50.  No flow
  sample appeared.  Changing the rate to 500 then gave the expected 4.
  So the flow sample yield is not always consistent with the configured rate across an enable
  and disable cycle: exact, 40 out of 2000, on the first enable, and zero on a later one at the
  same setting.  This run did not isolate it.
  => STEP 7 PASS: the repeat check ran four cycles and each one is reported with its numbers.
     Defect 1 did not reproduce.  Defect 2 appeared during the repeats.  Both are for a
     developer.  A re-test should run about ten cycles, with a counted burst and a capture in
     every window.

